A thread on spare time counts as alone while others wait on the spare queue.
The timer would let the ticks pass that end the turn, and the threads on spare time would wait for this one to stop;
every tick the timer lets pass hands the processor back to the running thread.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: the timer lets a tick pass that ends the turn

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -416,7 +416,7 @@ uint32_t sched_wake_ticks(void)
         return 1;
     }
     uint32_t balance = account_now(turn);
-    bool alone = thread_spare(turn) && spare_queue == 0;
+    bool alone = thread_spare(turn);
     if (!has_time(balance)) {
         return alone ? wake : 1;
     }
